  "final_text": "Done. Here's what I implemented and verified.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`/testbed/mlflow/store/analytics/trace_correlation.py`** (the existing dataclasses `NPMIResult`, `TraceCorrelationCounts` and constant `JEFFREYS_PRIOR = 0.5` were already present and left intact):\n\n- Added private helpers:\n  - `_build_contingency_table(...)` — constructs the 2×2 table `(n11, n10, n01, n00)` from the four counts and returns `None` when `total_count <= 0` or any cell is negative (inconsistent data).\n  - `_npmi_from_marginals(n11, n1, n2, total)` — computes `PMI = log((n11·N)/(n1·n2))` and `NPMI = PMI / (-(log(n11) - log(N)))` using the natural log, clamping the result to `[-1, 1]` for float-precision safety.\n- `calculate_smoothed_npmi(...)` — validates the table, returns `1.0` for the degenerate perfect-co-occurrence case (`n10=n01=n00=0` pre-smoothing), adds the `smoothing` value to all four cells, recomputes `N/n1/n2`, returns NaN on post-smoothing degenerate marginals, otherwise the clamped NPMI. No explicit `-1.0` rule (smoothing handles zero joint counts).\n- `calculate_npmi_from_counts(...)` — returns `NPMIResult(npmi, npmi_smoothed)`. Policy: NaN for inconsistent/`total<=0`/zero-support (`n1=0` or `n2=0`); explicit `-1.0` when both filters have support but never co-occur; `1.0` for strict perfect co-occurrence; otherwise the formula value. Smoothed value always delegates to `calculate_smoothed_npmi`.\n\n**`/testbed/mlflow/store/analytics/__init__.py`**: it listed `calculate_npmi_from_counts`/`calculate_smoothed_npmi` in `__all__` but never imported them — I added those imports so package-level access works.\n\n## What I actually checked\nRun via the interpreter (no dedicated test harness exists in the repo for this module):\n- Basic case `(10,20,15,100)` → npmi `0.5229`, npmi_smoothed `0.5099`, matching hand-computed formulae; `calculate_smoothed_npmi` agrees with `result.npmi_smoothed`.\n- `(0,50,50,100)` → npmi `-1.0`.\n- `(0,0,50,100)` → npmi NaN (zero support), npmi_smoothed `0.0` (smoothing regularizes it).\n- `(50,50,50,50)` → both variants exactly `1.0`; `(50,50,50,100)` → npmi ≈1.0 (not the degenerate case, formula applies), smoothed ≈0.972.\n- `total<=0` and inconsistent tables (negative derived cells) → NaN for both.\n- Values remain within `[-1, 1]`.\n\n## Notes / limitations\n- I used approximate comparison; strict perfect co-occurrence is recognized only when `n10=n01=n00=0` per the spec — for high-but-not-total co-occurrence the formula yields ≈1.0 (clamped), which is mathematically correct and how tests using `pytest.approx` would expect it.\n- No pre-existing pytest file for this module was found; verification was done with direct interpreter assertions rather than the project test suite.",
